  "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh, cleaned by scripts/bible_mirror.py). The mirror carries no Old Testament, so OT quotations reuse the wording of an already-shipped Amharic work where one quotes the same verse (source_file names it) and are otherwise self_rendered in the 1962 register. The English edition quotes the KJV; where the 1962 text differs, the 1962 wording was kept verbatim.",
  "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: an exact substring (at least 20 characters) of the 1962 NT verse, or (at least 25) of the cited corpus file, inside that block. Shorter, re-personed or adapted quotations are self_rendered, whatever the translator believed. Verses the mirror bridges into one partial entry (scripts/bible_mirror.py damaged.json) were not quoted from it.",
  "Torrey's own words quoted in this companion were ported from the shipped Amharic editions of his books (the-person-and-work-of-the-holy-spirit, baptism-with-the-holy-spirit, how-to-succeed-in-the-christian-life, how-to-bring-men-to-christ, the-fundamental-doctrines-of-the-christian-faith) and his Amharic biography where the passage matched; otherwise translated fresh."
